  - heading: Using Example Bars
    text: "This section shows you how to quickly use one of the many pre-built progress
      bars included in the asset.\n\u2022 Step 1: Complete the Setup\n\nBefore continuing,
      make sure you\u2019ve completed the #how-to-add-a-progress-bar section (you
      can skip creating new material, as we use one of the many pre-built materials
      that come with the asset. \n\nStep 2: Find Example Materials\n[[IMAGE:0]] \n[[IMAGE:1]]
      \n\nMaterials are in `Demo Files/Materials/`.\n\nUse the included feature and
      style materials. This checkout has no Canvas demo or script-usage demo material
      group.\n\nStep 3: Choose and Apply a Style\n\u2022 Pick a material you like
      from any folder.\n\u2022 Change its shader based on usage:\n\u2022 Canvas Shader
      \u2013 for UI images\n\u2022 Unlit Shader \u2013 for 3D objects (quads/planes)\n\u2022
      Assign that material in two places:\n\u2022 On the UI Image component (for
      canvas) or Mesh Renderer (for 3D)\n\u2022 In the ProceduralProgressBar script
      (Get Material or drag it in)\n[[IMAGE:2]] \n[[IMAGE:3]] \n[[IMAGE:4]] \n[[IMAGE:5]]
      \n[[IMAGE:6]] \n\nDone!\n\nYou now have a working example bar in your scene.\n[[IMAGE:7]] "
